{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "From Past to Present"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The California Gold Rush"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a light fold out bed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have only just finished my small cabin with a stove, a cot, so I am more comfortable at night than I was in the tent. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about digging for gold."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to strew"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spread or scatter without care"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Clothing of all descriptions has been strewn all over the ground as if it cost nothing at all."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " A hole or tunnel dug into the earth for the purpose of extracting ore."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Clothing of all descriptions has been left by those that have moved on, as expected, to mines further north."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "indiscriminately"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "thoughtlessly, without care"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People haven't wanted to pay for washing so far, so everything is discarded indiscriminately. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to lose heart"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to lose courage or to want to give up "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: But fear not Janey, I haven't lost my heart up to now. I know you are thinking of me with love as I think of you. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to amass"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to gather and save"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hide my gold as a squirrel does his winter food. Have you wondered what I've amassed until now?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le08ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le08ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbial Clause of Comparison: Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to describe how something happens or is done, you can use adverbial clauses of comparison."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adverbial clauses of comparison of manner are introduced by the relative adverb <span class=\"italic\">as.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The boy speaks <span class=\"strong\">as if he is sick</span>.</br> It all happened <span class=\"strong\">as I predicted</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Clothing of all descriptions has been strewn the ground as if it cost nothing at all. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "These are as odd times as I ever thought I might experience! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Out on the claim is as lonely a place as any man can stand."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know you are thinking of me with love as I think of you. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I hide my gold as a squirrel does his winter food. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect for Unusual Events"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect</span> tense in variety of ways, but it is always used to make a connection between the past and the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a story, you can use it to refer to events that happened very recently. In these cases, you use words like <span class=\"italic\">just</span>, <span class=\"italic\">only just</span> and <span class=\"italic\">recently</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:</br><span class=\"italic\"> Although I have just been here a while I am still learning how to survive in this strange atmosphere.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> in questions to ask about past experience or unusual events:  </br></br>For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">Have you wondered what I've amassed until now? </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice the use of the word <span class=\"italic\">ever</span> in questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You also use words such as <span class=\"italic\">yet</span>, <span class=\"italic\">up to now</span>, <span class=\"italic\">so far</span> and <span class=\"italic\">until now</span> when you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>, since these words and phrases refer to a period of time covering the past to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">There are times when I work that I have lifted my head to realize I haven't spoken a word so far that day! </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "(You use<span class=\"italic\"> yet</span> in negative statements and in questions)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you ever heard of the \u201cgold rush\u201d or the \u201cKlondike\u201d?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "So many people have arrived recently. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Here, I have only just finished my small cabin with a stove and a  cot."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Why have shirts that haven't been worn more than once up to now been thrown away? People haven't wanted to pay for washing so far. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I haven't seen anyone pick a piece up and take it up yet either. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I watch the movie White Fang."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I choose a scene in the film to retell."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take notes to prepare to retell the scene."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I retell the scene to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">White Fang</span> about a young man going to look for gold in the Yukon."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose a scene in the film that you enjoy the most."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes to prepare to retell the scene."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Retell the scene to a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about history and civilization."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can compare two related events or actions. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about an unusual or unique event in life.  "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you know about t